exteraless python plugin sdk, from https://github.com/exteraless/exteraless
commit 2587d6c15b8ff31543c7c8a062ed35a8494933a4, gpl-3.0, files copied from
TMessagesProj/src/main/python: base_plugin, plugin_settings, hook_utils, markdown_utils, client_utils,
android_utils, file_utils, intents, ui/, extera_utils/

elyx_runtime/ is copied from the same commit; its yaml import is answered by python/shim/yaml.py.

left out: dev_server, pip_controller (needs requests).
the sdk reaches the app through app.exteraless.plugins.PythonBridge and PluginServices and through java.jclass;
python/shim/ provides those three for ios.

local changes, both for zwylib: it names the plugin behind a call by the "ElyxPlugins/<id>/" segment of the path of the
calling file, which is where exteraGram runs the code of an .elyx archive from.
- elyx_runtime/loader.py: the namespace of an archive searches <plugins>/ElyxPlugins/<id>, the link the extraction keeps to
  <plugins>/.elyx_extracted/<id>/<hash>, instead of the hashed folder. without it the entry module of zwylib is src/main.py
  and every setting, async task and hook it registers belongs to a plugin called "main"
- extera_utils/plugin_loader.py: ElyxPlugins joins the markers that give the owner of a file by its path, so the code that
  runs from the link, and a library that neighbours import from there, is still the code of its plugin


local change for the ios 12 sandbox:
- extera_utils/audit_gate.py: _runtime_paths adds every path on its own, as given and resolved, and _is_runtime_file also compares the normalized path as given. one path the sandbox refuses to resolve used to empty the cached list, and a plugin's `import random` was then refused as a file open without the files permission
- extera_utils/audit_gate.py: frozen os in the embedded interpreter may have no __file__, so _runtime_paths uses the interpreter prefixes and sys.path without it

- client_utils.py: send_request lets the NotImplementedError of PluginServices.sendRequest through. the fallback to the connections manager answers every plugin with the same refusal of getConnectionsManager, and the text of the host, which names the request class that is not allowed, never reached the plugin

- base_plugin.py: BasePlugin.logger, a logging.Logger whose records go to self.log. the exteraGram sdk of 1.4.5 has it and story_scheduler calls it; this exteraless commit does not

local change found on a phone:
- extera_utils/plugin_loader.py: _sandboxed_open reads <plugins>/<id>.py from <plugins>/<id>.plugin when only the second exists. zwylib builds that name for every plugin (PluginUtils.get_plugin_path) and logged a FileNotFoundError traceback for each one

local changes from the reverse report of 2.2.0 (tests/python/test_sdk_fixes.py):
- android_utils.py: _plugin_mark only guards its preparation. an error raised by the callback inside the with passed into the except and the generator yielded a second time, which turned every failed callback into "generator didn't stop after throw()"
- extera_utils/plugin_loader.py: _unload_record also clears change_callbacks
- hook_utils.py: find_class fails closed. a guard_java_class that raises refuses the class; a loader that is not importable yet (the sdk used on its own) still means no guard
- client_utils.py: AccountClient.run_on_queue posts under hook_scope(self.account), so the work runs for the account of the client and not the one that happens to be current
- elyx_runtime/settings.py: clear_settings replaces the stored object with {} through the bridge; it used to write null into every key, which stayed listed
- elyx_runtime/metadata.py: a .py metainfo or locale file is parsed with ast and only literal top-level assignments are taken; nothing in it runs, since it is read before the person agreed to install. a value that is computed (1 + 2, a call) is skipped
- elyx_runtime/assets.py, elyx_runtime/loader.py: a "." or ".." segment in an asset name, in `main` or in a directory the refmap declares is refused, so an archive names nothing outside its own folder
